      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Exercise-induced ventricular tachycardia is a well-described arrhythmia most commonly associated with atherosclerotic coronary artery disease. The case reported here presents its association with a coronary arteriovenous fistula, which has not been previously reported in the literature."},
